{"dataset_id":"3992c811-8123-ef11-840a-00224802a4c1","name":"International Comparison Program 2021","dataset_unique_id":"0066092","archive_nid":null,"first_published":null,"created_on":null,"modified_on":"2024-06-07T20:12:36+00:00","identification":{"id":"3a92c811-8123-ef11-840a-00224802a4c1","title":"International Comparison Program 2021","ddh_urltitle":null,"subtitle":null,"description":"<p>Results from the International Comparison Program (Benchmark) 2021 cycle include data for the new reference year 2021, revised data for the previous reference year 2017, and purchasing power parities (PPPs) time series for 2018 to 2020.</p><p>2021 results are available for 176 participating economies and their aggregate regions. They cover 45 expenditure headings and provide several indicators for each heading, including PPPs, national accounts expenditures in PPP and nominal terms, and price level indices. Imputed results are available for an additional 19 economies that did not participate in the ICP 2021 cycle.</p><p>Revised 2017 results are available for 178 participating economies and cover 44 expenditure headings and several indicators, including PPPs, national accounts expenditures in PPP and nominal terms, and price level indices. Additionally, imputed results are available for 17 economies that did not participate in the ICP 2017 cycle.</p><p>Annual PPPs are available for 2017 to 2021 and cover 6 major expenditure headings.</p><p>2022-2023 GDP PPP series are also provided beyond the most recent ICP benchmark based on the standard extrapolation approach.</p>","acronym":"ICP","topics":[{"id":"bd689cd3-8323-ef11-840a-000d3a5a7181","name":"Economic Growth"},{"id":"bf689cd3-8323-ef11-840a-000d3a5a7181","name":"Macroeconomic and Structural Policies"},{"id":"c0689cd3-8323-ef11-840a-000d3a5a7181","name":"Poverty"}],"parent_dataset":null,"collection_id":[],"translated_title":null,"point_of_contact":[],"language_supported":[{"id":"c9689cd3-8323-ef11-840a-000d3a5a7181","code":"EN